---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const breadcrumbJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://freeqrcode-generator.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Guides', item: 'https://freeqrcode-generator.com/guides' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Create vCard QR Code', item: 'https://freeqrcode-generator.com/guides/how-to-create-a-vcard-qr-code' },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How to Create a vCard Digital Business Card QR Code"
  description="Master vCard QR code creation. Encode full contact profiles with name, phone, email, company, and address for 1-tap phone saving."
  canonical="https://freeqrcode-generator.com/guides/how-to-create-a-vcard-qr-code"
  jsonLd={breadcrumbJsonLd}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-16 space-y-8">
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-400" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-indigo-600">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <a href="/guides" class="hover:text-indigo-600">Guides</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 truncate">Create vCard QR Code</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="space-y-3">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight leading-tight">
        How to Create a vCard Digital Business Card QR Code
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono">Updated August 2026 • 4 min read</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-6 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
      <p>
        A <strong>vCard QR code</strong> encodes contact information using the universal RFC 6350 electronic business card standard. When scanned by an iPhone or Android camera, it instantly displays a "Create New Contact" prompt with all fields pre-populated.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-2">Static vCard vs Hosted Digital Business Card</h2>
      <p>
        You have two powerful options when creating contact QR codes:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>Static vCard:</strong> Encodes the raw vCard payload directly in the QR matrix. Works 100% offline without internet access.</li>
        <li><strong>Hosted Digital Business Card:</strong> Points to an interactive mobile web profile with your avatar, bio, and social links, plus a one-tap "Save Contact" button.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-2">Best Practices for High Scannability</h2>
      <p>
        Because vCard files contain multiple fields, keep non-essential notes concise to avoid overly dense QR grids. For dense codes, ensure you print at a minimum physical size of <strong>1.5 × 1.5 inches (38 × 38 mm)</strong>.
      </p>

      <div class="pt-4">
        <a href="/vcard-qr-code-generator" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-2xl font-bold text-xs bg-indigo-600 hover:bg-indigo-700 text-white shadow-md">
          Create vCard QR Code &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
